        },
        {
          "id": "5e",
          "path": "internal/domain/envelope/envelope.go",
          "lineNumber": 244,
          "lineContent": "return w.enc.Encode(env)",
          "title": "JSON Encoding",
          "description": "Serializes envelope to JSON with newline delimiter"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Envelope Writing with Validation Enforcement\n├── protocol.Write() entry \u003c-- 5a\n│   ├── protocol.Validate() call \u003c-- 5b\n│   │   ├── envelope.Validate() (base checks) \u003c-- internal/protocol/protocol.go:137\n│   │   ├── validateCASDigest() \u003c-- internal/protocol/protocol.go:142\n│   │   ├── validateCacheMetadata() \u003c-- internal/protocol/protocol.go:146\n│   │   ├── validateMemoryMetadata() \u003c-- internal/protocol/protocol.go:150\n│   │   └── validateErrorStatusCode() \u003c-- internal/protocol/protocol.go:154\n│   └── envelope.NewWriter() creation \u003c-- 5c\n│       └── NewWriter() constructor \u003c-- 5d\n│           ├── json.NewEncoder(w) \u003c-- internal/domain/envelope/envelope.go:238\n│           └── SetEscapeHTML(false) \u003c-- internal/domain/envelope/envelope.go:239\n└── Writer.Write() invocation\n    └── enc.Encode(env) \u003c-- 5e\n        └── JSON serialization to io.Writer",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nEvery skill execution in foxctl produces a **JSON envelope** as output—a standardized wrapper containing the result, metadata, and error information. Before these envelopes reach stdout or get persisted to disk, they must be **validated** to ensure they conform to the Core Profile v1 specification. Invalid envelopes could break downstream consumers, corrupt job history, or violate protocol contracts. The `protocol.Write()` function [5a] serves as the **validation gate**: it blocks any envelope that doesn't meet the spec from being written.\n\nThis matters because:\n- **Skills can be buggy** and produce malformed output\n- **Protocol extensions** (CAS digests, cache metadata) have consistency rules beyond basic JSON validity\n- **Multiple execution paths** (daemon, ephemeral, plugins) all need the same validation guarantees\n\n## Details\n\n### Two-Layer Validation\n\nThe system has **two validation layers**:\n\n1. **Base envelope validation** (`envelope.Validate()`) checks Core Profile v1 invariants: version must be 1, status must be \"ok\" or \"error\", timestamps must be RFC3339 UTC, error envelopes must have both code and message [1c-1f]\n\n2. **Protocol-level validation** (`protocol.Validate()`) [5b] extends base validation with four additional checks:\n   - **CAS digest consistency**: if `meta.cas_digest` is set, it must match `data.artifact` and use the `sha256:` prefix\n   - **Cache metadata**: if `meta.source` is \"cache\", then `meta.cache_key` must be present\n   - **Memory metadata**: if `meta.source` is \"memory\", then `meta.memory` must have name and type\n   - **Error status codes**: error envelopes with `data.summary.status_code` must have codes in the 400-599 range\n\n### Write-Time Enforcement\n\nThe `protocol.Write()` function [5a] enforces validation **before any I/O occurs**. The flow is:\n\n1. Call `protocol.Validate()` [5b] which runs all validation layers\n2. If validation fails, return error immediately—**nothing gets written**\n3. If validation passes, create a JSON encoder with `envelope.NewWriter()` [5c, 5d]\n4. The encoder is configured with `SetEscapeHTML(false)` for canonical output [5d]\n5. Finally, `enc.Encode(env)` [5e] serializes the envelope to JSON with a trailing newline\n\nThis **fail-fast approach** prevents invalid envelopes from polluting the system. The validation error includes the command name and status for debugging.\n\n### Real-World Usage\n\nEvery execution path uses this validation gate:\n- Job executor validates skill output before persisting results [6c]\n- Ephemeral execution validates before annotation [7c]\n- CLI validates daemon responses before trusting them [8b]\n- Plugin manager validates plugin responses before processing [from openapi/plugin/manager.go:360]\n\nThe consistency is critical: **one validation function, enforced everywhere**."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "title": "Real-World Usage: Skill Execution Result Validation",
      "description": "Storage/jobs executor - shows validation enforcement at skill execution boundaries",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "6a",
          "path": "internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 189,
          "lineContent": "func (e *Executor) executeSkill(ctx context.Context, opts executeOptions) ([]byte, error) {",
          "title": "Skill Execution Entry",
          "description": "Orchestrates skill execution with job state management"
        },
        {
          "id": "6b",
          "path": "internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 200,
          "lineContent": "ctx, traceID := observability.EnsureTraceID(ctx)",
          "title": "Observability Setup",
          "description": "Ensures trace ID exists for distributed tracing"
        },
        {
          "id": "6c",
          "path": "internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 376,
          "lineContent": "if validationErr := envelope.Validate(resultEnv); validationErr != nil {",
          "title": "Result Envelope Validation",
          "description": "Validates skill output envelope before persisting - catches malformed skill output"
        },
        {
          "id": "6d",
          "path": "internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 377,
          "lineContent": "wrapped := fmt.Errorf(\"envelope validation failed: %w\", validationErr)",
          "title": "Validation Error Wrapping",
          "description": "Wraps validation errors with context for debugging"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Skill Execution Pipeline (storage/jobs/executor)\n└── executeSkill() entry \u003c-- 6a\n    ├── Execution setup\n    │   ├── startExecution() - prep job dir/progress \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:190\n    │   └── observability.EnsureTraceID() \u003c-- 6b\n    ├── Skill runner invocation\n    │   └── skillExecutor.Execute() - runs skill \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:59\n    ├── Result processing\n    │   ├── json.Unmarshal(stdout, \u0026resultEnv) \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:370\n    │   └── envelope.Validate(resultEnv) \u003c-- 6c\n    │       └── validation failure handling \u003c-- 6d\n    │           ├── recordProgressFailure() \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:378\n    │           └── persist.UpdateState(StateError) \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:379\n    └── Success path\n        ├── persist.UpdateState(StateOK) \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:390\n        └── writeResultFile() \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:395",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nSkills in foxctl are isolated executables that process JSON input and emit JSON output. The **executor** must ensure that skills produce **valid envelopes** conforming to Core Profile v1 before persisting results to the job store. Invalid output from a skill could corrupt the job database, break downstream consumers, or hide execution failures. The validation at [6c] acts as a **critical boundary check** that catches malformed skill output before it propagates through the system.\n\n## Details\n\n### Execution Flow\n\nThe `executeSkill` function [6a] orchestrates the complete lifecycle of running a skill with persistent job state. It first sets up observability context [6b] to enable distributed tracing across the skill execution boundary. The skill binary runs in isolation (WASI or exec), producing stdout that should contain a valid JSON envelope.\n\n### Validation Checkpoint\n\nAfter the skill completes, the executor unmarshals the stdout into an envelope structure and **immediately validates it** [6c]. This validation enforces all Core Profile v1 invariants: version must be 1, status must be \"ok\" or \"error\", timestamps must be RFC3339 UTC, error envelopes must have both code and message, and success envelopes must not have error fields.\n\n### Failure Handling\n\nWhen validation fails [6d], the executor treats this as a **skill malfunction** rather than a normal error result. It records a progress failure event, updates the job state to `StateError` with the validation error message, and prevents the invalid envelope from being persisted. This protects the system from propagating corrupt data while preserving debugging information about what went wrong.\n\n### Success Path\n\nValid envelopes proceed to state updates (`StateOK`) and result file persistence, making them available for retrieval via `jobs result` commands and enabling cache hits for future identical requests."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "title": "Real-World Usage: Ephemeral Execution with Validation",
      "description": "Runservice ephemeral - shows validation in fast-path ephemeral execution mode",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "7a",
          "path": "internal/runservice/ephemeral.go",
          "lineNumber": 24,
          "lineContent": "func (e *Executor) ExecuteEphemeral(input []byte) error {",
          "title": "Ephemeral Execution Entry",
          "description": "Fast-path execution without job persistence for hooks and transient operations"
        },
        {
          "id": "7b",
          "path": "internal/runservice/ephemeral.go",
          "lineNumber": 120,
          "lineContent": "func (e *Executor) handleEphemeralSuccess(stdout []byte) error {",
          "title": "Success Handler",
          "description": "Processes successful ephemeral execution output"
        },
        {
          "id": "7c",
          "path": "internal/runservice/ephemeral.go",
          "lineNumber": 127,
          "lineContent": "if err := envelope.Validate(resultEnv); err != nil {",
          "title": "Ephemeral Result Validation",
          "description": "Validates envelope from ephemeral skill execution before annotation"
        },
        {
          "id": "7d",
          "path": "internal/runservice/ephemeral.go",
          "lineNumber": 132,
          "lineContent": "annotated := annotateCorrelationAndJob(stdout, \"\", e.options.CorrelationID)",
          "title": "Metadata Annotation",
          "description": "Adds correlation ID and ephemeral markers to envelope metadata"
        },
        {
          "id": "7e",
          "path": "internal/runservice/ephemeral.go",
          "lineNumber": 166,
          "lineContent": "meta[\"source\"] = \"ephemeral\"",
          "title": "Source Annotation",
          "description": "Marks envelope as coming from ephemeral execution path"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Ephemeral Execution Flow (Runservice)\n├── ExecuteEphemeral() entry \u003c-- 7a\n│   ├── TryServeCache() (cache read attempt) \u003c-- internal/runservice/ephemeral.go:26\n│   ├── skillExecutor.Execute() (run skill) \u003c-- internal/runservice/ephemeral.go:59\n│   └── handleEphemeralSuccess() \u003c-- 7b\n│       ├── json.Unmarshal(stdout, \u0026resultEnv) \u003c-- internal/runservice/ephemeral.go:124\n│       ├── envelope.Validate(resultEnv) \u003c-- 7c\n│       ├── annotateCorrelationAndJob() \u003c-- 7d\n│       │   └── annotateEphemeral() \u003c-- internal/runservice/ephemeral.go:133\n│       │       ├── meta[\"source\"] = \"ephemeral\" \u003c-- 7e\n│       │       └── meta[\"ephemeral\"] = true \u003c-- internal/runservice/ephemeral.go:167\n│       └── writeEnvelope(stdout, annotated) \u003c-- internal/runservice/ephemeral.go:136\n└── handleEphemeralError() (error path) \u003c-- internal/runservice/ephemeral.go:74\n    └── protocol.Write(stdout, errorEnv) \u003c-- internal/runservice/ephemeral.go:112",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\n**Ephemeral execution** is a fast-path mode for running skills without the overhead of job persistence. The problem: normal skill execution involves creating job records, opening SQLite stores, writing state updates, and capturing trajectories—adding ~150ms of latency. For transient operations like **git hooks** or **test watchers** that run frequently and don't need history, this overhead is wasteful. Ephemeral mode skips all persistence infrastructure, achieving **60% latency reduction** while still validating output and maintaining observability [7a].\n\n## Details\n\n### Execution Flow\n\nThe entry point `ExecuteEphemeral()` [7a] first attempts a **cache read** for deduplication (line 26), then executes the skill directly via `skillExecutor.Execute()` (line 59) without opening job stores. The skill runs in an isolated process with trace context propagated for observability.\n\n### Success Path Validation\n\nWhen execution succeeds, `handleEphemeralSuccess()` [7b] unmarshals the skill's stdout into an envelope structure (line 124), then **validates it** using `envelope.Validate()` [7c] to ensure the skill produced valid Core Profile v1 output. This validation is critical—it catches malformed skill output before it reaches the user.\n\n### Metadata Annotation\n\nAfter validation passes, the system annotates the envelope with execution context [7d]. The `annotateEphemeral()` function (line 133) adds **`meta.source = \"ephemeral\"`** [7e] and **`meta.ephemeral = true`** (line 167) to mark the result as coming from the fast path. This metadata helps distinguish ephemeral results from persisted job results in logs and debugging.\n\n### Output Emission\n\nFinally, `writeEnvelope()` (line 136) writes the annotated, validated envelope to stdout. Note that **cache writes are intentionally skipped**—this is where the latency savings come from. The result is ephemeral by design.\n\n### Error Handling\n\nIf execution fails, `handleEphemeralError()` (line 74) checks if the skill already returned an error envelope. If so, it passes it through. Otherwise, it constructs an error envelope with `protocol.Error()` using `ErrorCodeERuntime` and writes it via `protocol.Write()` (line 112), which performs validation before emission."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "title": "CLI Integration: Validation at Command Boundaries",
      "description": "CLI run command - shows validation enforcement when receiving daemon responses with fallback to ephemeral mode",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "8a",
          "path": "cmd/foxctl/cmd/run.go",
          "lineNumber": 243,
          "lineContent": "if unmarshalErr := json.Unmarshal(result.Output, \u0026env); unmarshalErr != nil {",
          "title": "Daemon Response Parsing",
          "description": "Attempts to parse daemon response as envelope"
        },
        {
          "id": "8b",
          "path": "cmd/foxctl/cmd/run.go",
          "lineNumber": 255,
          "lineContent": "if validateErr := protocol.Validate(env); validateErr != nil {",
          "title": "Daemon Response Validation",
          "description": "Validates daemon-returned envelope before trusting it"
        },
        {
          "id": "8c",
          "path": "cmd/foxctl/cmd/run.go",
          "lineNumber": 256,
          "lineContent": "fmt.Fprintf(cmd.ErrOrStderr(), \"daemon returned invalid envelope, falling back to ephemeral mode\\n\")",
          "title": "Validation Failure Fallback",
          "description": "Falls back to ephemeral execution if daemon returns invalid envelope"
        },
        {
          "id": "8d",
          "path": "cmd/foxctl/cmd/run.go",
          "lineNumber": 268,
          "lineContent": "_, err = stdout.Write(result.Output)",
          "title": "Validated Output Write",
          "description": "Writes validated envelope to stdout after all checks pass"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "CLI Run Command (foxctl run)\n└── runSkillCmd execution\n    ├── Daemon invocation attempt\n    │   └── Daemon returns result.Output\n    │       ├── JSON unmarshal attempt \u003c-- 8a\n    │       │   └── Parse to envelope struct \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/run.go:242\n    │       ├── Protocol validation \u003c-- 8b\n    │       │   ├── protocol.Validate(env)\n    │       │   │   ├── Base envelope.Validate() \u003c-- internal/protocol/protocol.go:137\n    │       │   │   └── Protocol extensions\n    │       │   │       ├── validateCASDigest() \u003c-- internal/protocol/protocol.go:142\n    │       │   │       ├── validateCacheMetadata() \u003c-- internal/protocol/protocol.go:146\n    │       │   │       ├── validateMemoryMetadata() \u003c-- internal/protocol/protocol.go:150\n    │       │   │       └── validateErrorStatusCode() \u003c-- internal/protocol/protocol.go:154\n    │       │   └── Validation failure detected\n    │       │       └── Fallback to ephemeral \u003c-- 8c\n    │       │           └── executor.ExecuteEphemeral() \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/run.go:253\n    │       └── Validation success\n    │           └── Write to stdout \u003c-- 8d\n    └── Direct ephemeral mode (if daemon unavailable)\n        └── executor.ExecuteEphemeral() \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/run.go:253",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen `foxctl run` executes a skill, it needs to ensure the output is a **valid envelope** before trusting it. Skills can be arbitrary executables (WASI or native), and they might crash, produce malformed JSON, or violate Core Profile v1 invariants. The CLI must **validate daemon responses** before passing them to users, with a fallback to direct execution if validation fails [8b, 8c].\n\nThis validation layer prevents corrupted or malicious envelopes from propagating through the system, ensuring that all downstream consumers (caching, memory storage, trajectory capture) can rely on envelope structure guarantees.\n\n## Details\n\n### Validation Entry Point\n\nThe `run` command receives output from either a daemon or direct execution [8a]. It first attempts to **unmarshal the JSON** into an `envelope.Envelope` struct. If unmarshaling fails, it falls back to ephemeral execution mode.\n\n### Two-Layer Validation\n\nAfter successful unmarshaling, the CLI invokes `protocol.Validate(env)` [8b], which performs:\n\n1. **Base validation** via `envelope.Validate()` - checks Core Profile v1 invariants: version=1, valid status (ok/error), required timestamps, error field consistency\n2. **Protocol extensions** - four additional checks:\n   - `validateCASDigest()` ensures `meta.cas_digest` matches `data.artifact` when present\n   - `validateCacheMetadata()` requires `meta.cache_key` when `meta.source=\"cache\"`\n   - `validateMemoryMetadata()` requires `meta.memory` reference when `meta.source=\"memory\"`\n   - `validateErrorStatusCode()` ensures error envelopes have status codes in 400-599 range\n\n### Fallback Strategy\n\nIf validation fails, the CLI **prints a warning** and switches to ephemeral execution mode [8c], bypassing the daemon entirely. This ensures users always get valid output, even if the daemon is misbehaving. The fallback calls `executor.ExecuteEphemeral(input)` which runs the skill directly in-process.\n\n### Success Path\n\nWhen validation passes, the CLI writes the envelope directly to stdout [8d]. At this point, the envelope is guaranteed to be valid and can be safely consumed by other `foxctl` commands via piping or stored in the job/cache/memory systems."
    }
  ],
  "description": "Maps the canonical JSON envelope format (Core Profile v1) from base types through protocol-level validation extensions to real-world usage. The system has two layers: base envelope validation in domain/envelope and protocol-level extensions in internal/protocol. Key validation entry points include [2a] for protocol validation and [5a] for write-time validation, with real usage shown in [6c] and [7c].",
  "mermaidDiagram": "graph TB\n    subgraph BaseEnv[\"Base Envelope System\"]\n        style BaseEnv fill:#eebefa\n        1a[\"1a: OK Constructor\"]\n        1b[\"1b: Timestamp Init\"]\n        1c[\"1c: Base Validate\"]\n        1e[\"1e: Status Check\"]\n        1f[\"1f: Timestamp Parse\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph ProtocolVal[\"Protocol Validation Hub\"]\n        style ProtocolVal fill:#d0bfff\n        2a[\"2a: Protocol Validate\"]\n        2b[\"2b: Call Base\"]\n        2c[\"2c: CAS Validate\"]\n        2d[\"2d: Cache Meta\"]\n        2e[\"2e: Memory Meta\"]\n        2f[\"2f: Error Code\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph CASVal[\"CAS Digest Validation\"]\n        style CASVal fill:#b2f2bb\n        3a[\"3a: validateCASDigest\"]\n        3b[\"3b: Extract Artifact\"]\n        3c[\"3c: Extractor Entry\"]\n        3e[\"3e: Prefix Check\"]\n        3f[\"3f: Digest Match\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph ErrorHandling[\"Error Envelope Creation\"]\n        style ErrorHandling fill:#ffec99\n        4a[\"4a: Protocol Error\"]\n        4c[\"4c: Base Error\"]\n        4d[\"4d: Error Fields\"]\n        4e[\"4e: Error Codes\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Writing[\"Output \u0026 Writing\"]\n        style Writing fill:#ffd8a8\n        5a[\"5a: Protocol Write\"]\n        5b[\"5b: Pre-Write Validate\"]\n        5d[\"5d: Writer Create\"]\n        5e[\"5e: JSON Encode\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph SkillExec[\"Skill Execution\"]\n        style SkillExec fill:#99e9f2\n        6a[\"6a: Execute Skill\"]\n        6c[\"6c: Result Validate\"]\n        6d[\"6d: Error Wrap\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph EphemeralExec[\"Ephemeral Execution\"]\n        style EphemeralExec fill:#a5d8ff\n        7a[\"7a: Execute Ephemeral\"]\n        7b[\"7b: Success Handler\"]\n        7c[\"7c: Result Validate\"]\n        7e[\"7e: Source Annotate\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph CLIInteg[\"CLI Integration\"]\n        style CLIInteg fill:#fcc2d7\n        8a[\"8a: Parse Response\"]\n        8b[\"8b: Validate Response\"]\n        8c[\"8c: Fallback\"]\n        8d[\"8d: Write Output\"]\n    end\n\n    1a --\u003e|sets timestamp| 1b\n    1b --\u003e|feeds into| 1c\n    1c --\u003e|checks status| 1e\n    1c --\u003e|parses ts| 1f\n\n    2a --\u003e|calls first| 2b\n    2b --\u003e|delegates to| 1c\n    2a --\u003e|validates| 2c\n    2a --\u003e|validates| 2d\n    2a --\u003e|validates| 2e\n    2a --\u003e|validates| 2f\n\n    2c --\u003e|calls| 3a\n    3a --\u003e|extracts| 3b\n    3b --\u003e|uses| 3c\n    3a --\u003e|checks prefix| 3e\n    3a --\u003e|compares| 3f\n\n    4a --\u003e|creates| 4c\n    4c --\u003e|sets| 4d\n    4a --\u003e|uses| 4e\n\n    5a --\u003e|validates via| 2a\n    5a --\u003e|writes via| 5d\n    5b --\u003e|enforces| 2a\n    5d --\u003e|encodes| 5e\n\n    6a --\u003e|produces| 6c\n    6c --\u003e|validates with| 1c\n    6c --\u003e|wraps errors| 6d\n\n    7a --\u003e|calls| 7b\n    7b --\u003e|validates| 7c\n    7c --\u003e|validates with| 1c\n    7c --\u003e|annotates| 7e\n\n    8a --\u003e|parses to| 8b\n    8b --\u003e|validates with| 2a\n    8b --\u003e|fails to| 8c\n    8b --\u003e|succeeds to| 8d\n\n    2a -.-\u003e|hub for| 5a\n    2a -.-\u003e|hub for| 6c\n    2a -.-\u003e|hub for| 7c\n    2a -.-\u003e|hub for| 8b"
}